       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't solve either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, about twice metformin's maximum daily dose. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The order still has to come from a prescriber.** A medication order needs authorization from a licensed clinician who is responsible for this patient. Approval from hospital leadership can't replace that.\n\nThe patient's attending physician or the medicine team should decide the regimen and enter the order. If they really do want a dose above the usual maximum, they can enter it themselves with a documented clinical reason, and pharmacy would normally review it. I can help a prescriber enter the order once they've confirmed it."
